ret = nvif_outp_dp_aux_xfer(&nv_encoder->outp,
			    msg->request, &size, msg->address, msg->buffer);
Reason: This call is made without checking if the device is runtime suspended, causing a crash in GSP code when the device is asleep.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
if (pm_runtime_suspended(nv_connector->base.dev->dev))
    return -EBUSY;
Reason: This check prevents AUX transfers when the device is suspended, returning -EBUSY instead of proceeding to the GSP code that would crash.

